  "revision_note_20260911_remote": "Remote review: the framing guards removed from scripts/audit_paper1_integrity.py were restored and now run ahead of this candidate's numeric audit; the superseded candidate_20260905 and candidate_20260905_maf packages were moved to archives/submission_candidates/ so submission/ holds one package; reproduction input records were carried into this package. No displayed value changed.",
  "revision_note_20260911_remote_2": "Copy-edit and figure pass: every bare P italicised in the manuscript and cover letter (50 occurrences of *P*); Figures 1-2 rebuilt; documents rebuilt. No displayed value changed.",
  "revision_note_20260912_external_review": "External review round 8. Accepted and applied: TSHR BBJ prior sensitivity stated in the abstract and the opening Discussion; PP.H3 added to Table 2 so the distinct-variant and unresolved readings rest on displayed numbers; the '81 comparisons crossed the 0.80 threshold' sentence rewritten as a classification statement with its 9x3x3 decomposition; per-locus variant counts (1,479-7,740) and the purpose of the BBJ-plus-FinnGen criterion stated in Methods; the reconstructed exposure unit defined as approximately one standard deviation; gene-specific 80% detection limits reported, showing the IGF1R estimate fell below its own limit in all three outcomes; 'modest IGF1R contribution' widened to 'inherited contribution' because the FinnGen CI reaches 2.33; MAPKAPK5 given three decimals in a footnote; the 1000 Genomes panel given its own citation (new reference 18, all later references renumbered). Rejected after checking the data: no re-analysis was needed for colocalization input, which used unfiltered regional statistics (eQTL P up to 1.0; 1,479-7,740 variants per comparison). The UKB log-odds rescaling formula and the FinnGen 858/499,490 counts were already correct and documented.",
